--- explained
Target red: test 32 (a watcher step between the rename and the approval holds the put-back copy). Also red: test 20, both subtests. Its move fails on the second entry, so with approval moved after the moves the restore's checked/approved pair is never written, and the test asserts that pair before the compensating events.
Collateral, in every log: 11 FAIL lines from tests/test_action.py CanaryActionTests. Any edit under canary/ changes a file scanner/manifest.json hashes, so scripts/action.py scanner_manifest() exits 2 with "the bundled scanner failed its integrity check" (quoted in the tracebacks below). Five of the class's six methods go red (11 FAIL lines with subtests); the sixth, test_an_unlisted_module_in_a_subfolder_is_refused, expects exit 2 and stays green.

